group: Cs
formula: CH4O
construction: Fragment orbitals (extended Hückel)
headline: 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · labels in C<sub>s</sub>\n1 empty model orbital lies more than 30 eV above the HOMO; it is drawn at the top of the axis (marked ↑) with the model energy beside it.\n4 model levels have no close calculated counterpart (overlap below 0.80); read its calculated energy with care.
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (C and H4O). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the narrow column on the right. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, its energy in Hartree and the overlap value (1 is identical). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\n**Total electrons: 14** (C 4, H4O 10).\n\nThe grey bars are model levels that sit almost entirely on the H4O and take no part in the interaction; they are counted, not drawn.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in Cs; the code reported none.\n\n**Picked atoms.** One atom is drawn against the atoms bonded to it; two bonded atoms cut that bond and the two sides are drawn against each other (in and out of phase when they are equal). A metal gives the fragment-orbital diagram, each ligand being a connected piece left when the metal is removed. A single atom that is not a metal is drawn the same way when it is not fixed by every symmetry operation of the molecule, or when atoms are bonded to neither it nor its neighbours: the atom against the connected pieces left when it is removed, each piece neutral.
verdict: differs The model puts 11A'* below 3A''*, the model puts 11A'* below 10A'*, the model puts 11A'* below 8A'*; your calculation has those the other way round (9 of 45 pairs of the 10 valence orbitals (overlap 0.67–0.98)).
